# the changes game mutants lets by, one per line as NAME :: WHY.
pzm/help.go toolHelp: wide := 0 => wide := 1 :: every verb name has at least one letter, so the widest is never under one, and with no verbs nothing is padded
pzm/help.go flagLines: wide := 0 => wide := 1 :: every flag's usage is its long form, at least three characters, so the widest is never under one, and with no flags nothing is written
verb/facts.go package: LeavesAlone Existing = iota + 1 // adds, if anything => LeavesAlone Existing = iota + 2 // adds, if anything :: the values start above zero only so the zero value is not a statement; from two the zero value is still none of them, and nothing reads the numbers, only the names
verb/facts.go package: ThisMachine Reach = iota + 1 // stays on it => ThisMachine Reach = iota + 2 // stays on it :: the values start above zero only so the zero value is not a statement; from two the zero value is still none of them, and nothing reads the numbers, only the names
verb/facts.go package: NoOne Person = iota + 1 // runs alone => NoOne Person = iota + 2 // runs alone :: the values start above zero only so the zero value is not a statement; from two the zero value is still none of them, and nothing reads the numbers, only the names
verb/facts.go package: Light Load = iota + 1 // never holds a core => Light Load = iota + 2 // never holds a core :: the values start above zero only so the zero value is not a statement; from two the zero value is still none of them, and nothing reads the numbers, only the names
verb/check.go givesDryRun: found = found || each.Kind == token.STRING && err == nil && text == "--dry-run" => found = found || (each.Kind == token.STRING || err == nil) && text == "--dry-run" :: only a string literal unquotes to "--dry-run": a char unquotes to one rune and a number does not unquote, so once the text matches the kind and the error add nothing
